      "OLED/QLED TV Repair Faults Explained",
      "OLED/QLED TV diagnosis should be slower and more careful because premium display symptoms can overlap. Black patches, color shift, dimming, vertical lines, HDMI faults and smart processor failures must be separated from true panel damage before any expensive decision is made.",
      "OLED TV Vertical Line Repair",
      "Vertical lines on an OLED display need careful panel, driver and board diagnosis. Pressure, impact and whether menus show the same line are useful details.",
      "QLED TV Dim Screen Repair",
      "QLED brightness loss may involve picture settings, local dimming, backlight electronics, power behavior or the display assembly, so diagnosis should precede a costly decision.",
      "OLED TV Color Issue Repair",
      "Color shift, dark patches and uneven tones can be source-specific, software-related or panel-level. Testing menus and multiple inputs helps narrow the issue.",
      "QLED TV No Display Repair",
      "A QLED television with power but no usable image may have input, mainboard, power, backlight or panel symptoms. Model-specific inspection is important.",
      "OLED QLED TV Mainboard Repair",
      "Boot loops, frozen apps, missing HDMI inputs and intermittent display behavior can involve the mainboard. Software and connected devices are checked before board work.",
      "OLED TV Burn In Inspection",
      "Persistent logos or uneven image retention need a realistic panel assessment. Content tests help separate temporary retention, settings and permanent panel wear.",
      "QLED TV Brightness Issue Diagnosis",
      "Uneven or reduced brightness can involve picture settings, local dimming, backlight control, power or panel behavior. Testing standard content helps compare zones safely.",
      "Safe handling",
      "Premium OLED and QLED panels are sensitive to pressure, heat and poor handling. GR Solution focuses on safe movement, careful visual inspection and practical repair feasibility before recommending board work or panel-related guidance.",
